Rationale (Linux-like copyleft, not MIT)
----------------------------------------
The Linux kernel uses the GPL family (GPL-2.0) so improvements stay free
software. This operators' console follows the same tradition with
**GPL-3.0-or-later**: strong copyleft for a userspace application, FSF’s
current GPL for new projects. Permissive MIT was intentionally rejected for
this product so derivatives and redistributed binaries remain open source.

